          "source_quote": "καὶ ὡς ἰδίᾳ χαριζόμενος ἐπιθυμίᾳ τὴν τοῦ θεοῦ βούλησιν ἐκτελεῖ",
          "english_quote": "and, while gratifying his own desire, carries out God’s will.",
          "issue": "The merely temporal “while” does not adequately preserve the characterization marked by ὡς with the participle. It also obscures the parallel with καὶ αὐτὸς δὲ ὡς ἑαυτῷ χαριζόμενος, rendered later as “and he too, as though gratifying himself.” The Greek need not imply that gratification is unreal, but both constructions expressly present the action under the description of self-gratification.",
          "suggested_revision": "Compare the source-transparent rendering “and, as one gratifying his own desire, carries out God’s will,” with a corresponding treatment of the later construction: “and he too, as one gratifying himself, offers God thanks for them.” Explain in a note whether ὡς is understood as subjective characterization or as “as though”; do not imply that the latter necessarily denies actual gratification. Any revised wording requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
