      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "παρὰ δὲ τὸ μέτρον ἐξελθὼν καὶ ἑαυτῷ τὴν κρίσιν λαβὼν ἀσεβεῖ.",
          "english_quote": "but one who goes beyond the proper measure and takes judgment upon himself acts impiously.",
          "issue": "The main English can preserve the ambiguity, but the lexical note presents assuming authority to judge or punish as the meaning without acknowledging the materially different possibility of receiving or incurring judgment for oneself. The preceding discussion of being judged and punished makes that alternative contextually viable. This is an interpretive-disclosure issue, not a defect requiring verification of the already checked print.",
